  "documentation": {
    "platform": "# Acme Platform\n\nAcme Platform is an event-driven commerce system of 6 services. Traffic enters through the [[gateway]], which routes to [[order]] and [[catalog]]. Asynchronous work fans out over [[eventbus|Kafka]].\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Product discovery and catalog management\n- Order placement and lifecycle\n- Payment authorization and capture\n- Customer notifications and analytics\n\n## Checkout\n```\nGateway → Order Service → Payment Service → Orders DB → order.completed\n```\n\n## Product browse\n```\nGateway → Catalog Service → Inventory Service\n```",
    "order": "# Order Service\n\nOrder Service owns the complete order lifecycle. It calls [[payment]] for payment authorization, persists state in [[ordersdb]], and publishes lifecycle events consumed by [[notification]] and [[analytics]].\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Creates and manages orders\n- Coordinates payments\n- Stores order state\n- Publishes lifecycle events\n\n## Create Order\n```\nPOST /orders → validate → authorize payment → save → publish order.completed\n```",
    "payment": "# Payment Service\n\nPayment Service authorizes, captures and refunds payments. It is called synchronously by [[order]] and delegates card processing to [[stripe]].\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Authorizes payments\n- Captures and refunds\n- Stores payment ledger\n- Emits payment events\n\n## Authorize\n```\nPOST /payments/authorize → risk check → Stripe intent → persist → publish payment.completed\n```",
    "process-order": "# processOrder()\n\nCoordinates checkout in `OrderService`. Called by [[create-order|OrderController.createOrder()]].\n\n## Execution\n- Calls [[validate-order]] and [[calculate-total]].\n- Authorizes payment through [[authorize-payment]].\n- Persists with [[save-order]].\n- Publishes [[order-completed]] through [[publish-order]].",
    "create-order": "# createOrder()\n\nHandles [[order-api]] and delegates to [[process-order]].",
    "order-service-class": "# OrderService\n\nImplements [[order-usecase]] and owns checkout orchestration. Open [[process-order]] to inspect callers and callees."
  }
}
